  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 25/01/06, the erection of a single storey rear extension measuring 67.26 cubic metres  was  lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\nThe development falls within the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class A of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 because  it is less than 70 cubic metres in volume and there are no previous extensions to the house, it is less than 4 metres high, is not nearer the highway than the nearest part of the original house, does not result in more than half the land around the original house being covered in extensions and the building is not listed.\r\n"
